{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the length of the median \\( BM \\) in the right triangle \\( \\triangle ABC \\) where \\( AB = 4\\sqrt{2} \\) and \\( BC = 2 \\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the right angle and the hypotenuse:**\n   Since \\( AB \\) and \\( BC \\) are the legs of the right triangle, \\( \\angle ABC \\) is the right angle. The hypotenuse is \\( AC \\).\n\n2. **Calculate the length of the hypotenuse \\( AC \\):**\n   Using the Pythagorean theorem:\n   \\[\n   AC = \\sqrt{AB^2 + BC^2} = \\sqrt{(4\\sqrt{2})^2 + 2^2} = \\sqrt{32 + 4} = \\sqrt{36} = 6\n   \\]\n\n3. **Determine the coordinates of the vertices:**\n   Place \\( B \\) at the origin \\((0, 0)\\), \\( A \\) at \\((4\\sqrt{2}, 0)\\), and \\( C \\) at \\((0, 2)\\).\n\n","prefix_end":686,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,3084,315,279,22553,17767,19800,1124,8,304,279,1290,21495,17767,1124,55114,19360,1124,8,1380,17767,14137,284,220,19,59,26888,90,17,92,1124,8,323,17767,18040,284,220,17,1124,701,582,686,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,28301,1437,279,1290,9210,323,279,9751,65628,810,25,1019,256,8704,17767,14137,1124,8,323,17767,18040,1124,8,525,279,14201,315,279,1290,21495,11,17767,1124,4044,19360,1124,8,374,279,1290,9210,13,576,9751,65628,810,374,17767,10584,1124,3593,17,13,3070,47866,279,3084,315,279,9751,65628,810,17767,10584,1124,1648,1019,256,12091,279,5355,95362,45195,57817,510,256,1124,9640,256,10584,284,1124,26888,90,1867,61,17,488,18040,61,17,92,284,1124,26888,96065,19,59,26888,90,17,5410,61,17,488,220,17,61,17,92,284,1124,26888,90,18,17,488,220,19,92,284,1124,26888,90,18,21,92,284,220,21,198,256,1124,2533,18,13,3070,35,24308,279,13934,315,279,17228,25,1019,256,10771,17767,425,1124,8,518,279,6238,1124,1188,15,11,220,15,10699,701,17767,362,1124,8,518,1124,1188,19,59,26888,90,17,2137,220,15,10699,701,323,17767,356,1124,8,518,1124,11